    "result": "I implemented `encode` and `decode` in `solution.py` and wrote a pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`. The suite passes (319 tests) with `python -m pytest -q tests`. `encode` splits the input into maximal runs with `itertools.groupby`, writes runs of four or more as `~n~c`, and doubles tildes in short runs. `decode` walks the string left to right, using a helper `_read_run` to parse counts and reject leading zeros, counts below 4, and a missing `~` or character. The tests cover the spec examples, every error case listed in the spec, and seeded random round-trips. I did not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation, or bandit gates. The code is small and every branch is exercised by the tests, but those gates have not been checked. Nothing was installed, and no files were created outside `solution.py` and `tests/`.",
